  "text" : "A batch is just a bunch of samples packed into one tensor so the GPU can parallelize.\nAnd a pi-towards training loop is what happens to that one batch.\nThe data loader yields it, the batch goes into the forward pass, and the model makes\na prediction.\nWe compare that prediction to the target, and that's the loss.\nThe loss is then propagated backwards, and the weights are updated as part of gradient\ndescent.\nThat is one training step.\nThen we go back to the data loader for the next batch.\nAnd epoch is one pass through the whole dataset.\nSo this inner loop runs once per epoch, and the outer loop runs for as many epochs as\nyou set.\nThe model never sees your dataset, it only ever sees one batch at a time.\nSo if your loss isn't moving, check the batch first.\nEverything downstream of it is the same four lines every time."
}
